1435 071600*       /       SUBROUTINE  TO  SET HIGH-ORDER BITS IN CP 13705 AND 13707.  BIT[4] IS  SET  IN
1436 071600*       /       13705;   BITS[4-5] ARE SET IN 13707.  THIS MAKES THE LINES INTO DOUBLE-HEIGHT,
1437 071600*       /       DOUBLE WIDTH UPPER AND LOWER HALVES RESPECTIVELY.  THIS ROUTINE DEPENDS ON THE
1438 071600*       /       PREVIOUS CONTENTS OF THE BITS BEING ZERO.
1439 071600*       
1440 071600* 0000  SET2,   .-.                             /SET HIGH BITS IN 2 WORDS ROUTINE
1441 071601* 6211          CDF     10                      /GOTO BUFFER FIELD
1442 071602* 1612          TAD I   L3705/(3705)            /GET CURRENT CONTENTS OF 13705
1443 071603* 1110          TAD     Z200/[200]              /ADD ON A HIGH-ORDER BIT
1444 071604* 3612          DCA I   L3705/(3705)            /STORE BACK
1445 071605* 1613          TAD I   L3707/(3707)            /GET CURRENT CONTENTS OF 13707
1446 071606* 1214          TAD     L300/(300)              /ADD ON HIGH-ORDER BITS
1447 071607* 3613          DCA I   L3707/(3707)            /STORE BACK
1448 071610* 6271          CDF     70                      /BACK TO OUR FIELD
1449 071611* 5600          JMP I   SET2                    /RETURN
